 "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 12852, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.agent_message_chunk", "role": "figtab-repo", "actor": "figtab-repo", "execution_id": "ffbe3f7884f4340b89a3194a68cf3c81", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "message (101 chunks)", "shown": {"message": "The venue answer (`venue-repo`#2) is in, and the figure code now exports at NeurIPS 2026 size. There are still no real figures, because `experiment-repo` hasn't delivered result files. The Fig. 2 and Fig. 3 outputs I checked came from a fake data set kept outside the repo.\n\n- **Geometry:** `figs/venue.py` is set to the venue's numbers: 5.5 in single column and a 7 pt minimum for figure text. It also records the venue's 8 pt floor for table text. Fig. 2 prints at 5.5 × 3.2 in, under the venue's 4 in ceiling for it. After shortening Fig. 3 to fit the venue's per-row height (aspect 0.45), the font check on its fake-data output reads 7.0 pt minimum with embedded TrueType.\n- **Main-text plan:** Figs. 1–5, with Fig. 6 as a table, to stay inside the venue's 6-figure, 3-table budget. Tables 1, 2 and 4 stay in the main text if pages allow, and Tables 3 and 5 and the robustness table go to the appendix. This is on `figtab-repo`#2 and pushed to `main`.\n- **Venue conventions:** captions go below figures and above tables, `booktabs` tables, and a second channel besides colour. The latter is already in place as markers and line styles.\n\nNext step is unchanged: when `experiment-repo` answers #2, I build the remaining figures and tables and deliver the finished PDFs to `paper-repo` `dev`."}}, {"id": "f72e030b-bd03-55f6-b101-62fbd4f09145", "at": 1795624071.2019298, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 12954, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "figtab-repo", "actor": "figtab-repo", "execution_id": "ffbe3f7884f4340b89a3194a68cf3c81"